# Waypoint Types

`Waypoint::Type` is in `src/Engine/Waypoint/Waypoint.hpp` and ends with
`COUNT`. Display names live in one table, `waypoint_type_names[]` in
`src/Dialogs/Waypoint/WaypointInfoWidget.cpp`
(`static_assert` against `COUNT`). `WaypointTypeLabel()` returns the
untranslated string. `GetWaypointTypeName()` translates it.

CUP styles live in one table, `see_you_styles[]` in
`src/Waypoint/SeeYouStyle.hpp`. The reader and the writer both use it.
The first row for a type is what the writer emits. Later rows are
read aliases. Thermal hotspots have no CUP style.

## Adding a new `Waypoint::Type`

Add it before `COUNT`. Then:

1. **Display name** — one `N_()` in `waypoint_type_names[]`, in enum
   order. The editor dropdown is built from this table, so it picks
   the new type up. Reuse an existing English string when there is one.
2. **CUP style** — one row in `see_you_styles[]`. The
   `static_assert` fails until every type except `THERMAL_HOTSPOT`
   is listed. Read aliases are extra rows for the same type.
3. **Map icon** — only if it should not use the turnpoint icon:
   - `src/Look/WaypointLook.hpp` / `.cpp`
   - `Data/resources.txt`
   - a `case` in `src/Renderer/WaypointIconRenderer.cpp`
     (the switch has no `default`, so a new type does not compile
     until it has a case)
4. **Search filter** — either add it to `specific_type_filters[]` in
   `src/Dialogs/Waypoint/WaypointList.cpp` (label comes from
   `WaypointTypeLabel()`) or to `category_waypoint_types[]` when an
   existing category already covers it. Also add the `TypeFilter`
   value and a `CompareType()` case. Both `static_assert`s in that
   file must stay true.
5. **Visibility threshold** *(rare)* —
   `src/Projection/MapWindowProjection.cpp`, only when the type
   needs a non-default scale.

## Adding a `TypeFilter` value

`enum class TypeFilter` is in `src/Waypoint/WaypointFilter.hpp`.

1. Add the value before `COUNT`, and keep it below
   `_DYNAMIC_FILE_ID_START` (100).
2. `WaypointFilter::CompareType()` — add the `case`.
3. `type_filter_choices[]` for a category, or
   `specific_type_filters[]` for one waypoint type.
   `FILE` stays out of both; loaded files are added at runtime.

## Translations

A new English label is an `N_()` in `waypoint_type_names[]`. Run
`make update-po` and commit the catalogs at the end of the branch.
